A||||3||Brian84SE||rebuilt short block||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||08-23-2000||09:10 PM||||Has anyone had any experience buying a short block over the internet?  Any recommendations as far as what company to go to?<BR>Anyone ever buy from a company called Blue Chip Motors?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||08-23-2000||09:19 PM||||I would recomend NOT buying a rebuilt short block. I've had two rebuilt engines, one lasted 20k miles before blowing a hole through a piston, and the second went 12k miles before siezing a wrist pin. I'm not the only one who's had problems. Next time I'll rebuild it myself! The thing I don't understand is how they can sell rebuilt engines for way less money than it would cost me for just the parts. That should tell you something about the quality of their rebuilds. I've never heard of Blue Chip Motors, but I believe you don't get more than you pay for.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||13
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||08-24-2000||10:11 AM||||I came to the same decision a few months ago. buy a rebuilt w/ no warenty, or rebuild my engine... well, my engine is in the shop now. more expencive, but it's getting a bunch of extra work, and I'll walk away w/ a warenty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-24-2000||12:13 PM||||Quality of rebuilds depends entirely on who's doing it. Many rebuilder shops DO give warrantees.<P>I've had rebuilt motors from such shops. It's a matter of finding good shops. The last one I had was in my Pinto for thousands of miles. I put it into 2 diferant cars before I finally wore it out.<P>I wouldn't do a short block unless I knew the heads where in really great shape. I'd rather have heads that are a package with the block. Then if the thing dies under warrantee I can just get a whole nother long block. Much less problem. With a short block they can argue you did the heads wrong and caused the problems.<P>Another option are the crate motors. They often aren't that much more than rebuilding and nearly always have good warrantee. You can order crates about any way you want and they pretty much drop in and go. Chances of a problem with a crate are pretty low.||||reg||1
